 {"success": true, "name": "arc-grid-reasoning", "file": "references/demo-driven-inference.md", "content": "# Demo-driven inference and submission feedback\n\n## Treat examples as constraints\n\nFor every example, make a compact before/after change list: `(row, column): old → new`. Also note the unchanged large objects. Infer the operation on a structural level, such as “remove isolated marker-color pixels embedded in a filled region,” rather than “recolor these particular cells.” Check that the structural rule predicts every changed and unchanged cell.\n\n## Distinguish anomalies from objects\n\nA singleton, a minority color, or a cell unlike its neighbors is not automatically noise. Compare its topology and context to changed pixels in the demo. A color can have multiple roles (object, marker, background) and the same apparent anomaly can be meaningful in another location. Preserve ambiguous structures until the demonstrated rule supports modifying them.\n\n## After an incorrect submission\n\nThe feedback only rules out the complete output; it does not identify which cell was wrong. Avoid making a succession of nearly identical guesses that toggle one ambiguous pixel while leaving an unverified global hypothesis intact. Instead:\n\n1. Re-evaluate the rule against every demo.\n2. Audit the submitted grid for all predicted edits and accidental edits.\n3. List plausible alternative rules and the observations that distinguish them.\n4. If the ambiguity materially affects many cells, request a demo when its information value justifies the fixed cost; otherwise submit the best evidence-backed candidate.\n5. Keep a coordinate-level record of what changed between attempts to avoid repeating a hypothesis.\n\n## Pre-submit validation\n\n- Preserve grid dimensions and all unaffected cells.\n- Confirm each changed cell has a reason linked to a demonstrated rule.\n- Verify row widths and values are in range.\n- Reconstruct the complete answer from the input plus an explicit edit list, rather than relying on visual memory.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-medium-fresh0/frozen/seen-reference/play/users/u075/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/arc-grid-reasoning/references/demo-driven-inference.md"}

